Fix pread_disk_io teardown: destroy m_fence_flush before m_file_pool

pread_storage holds a reference to the disk io's file_pool and calls
m_pool.release() (which locks the pool's internal mutex) from its
destructor. Members are destroyed in reverse declaration order, so with
m_fence_flush declared before m_file_pool the fence-flush vector is
destroyed AFTER the file pool. When a session is aborted while a fence
flush is still queued (e.g. save_resume_data(flush_disk_cache) in
flight), the leftover storage is destroyed after the pool, and the
destructor locks the pool's already-destroyed mutex:

    libc++abi: terminating due to uncaught exception of type
    std::__1::system_error: mutex lock failed: Invalid argument

Declare m_fence_flush after m_file_pool so any storage still queued at
teardown is destroyed while the pool is alive.

--- a/src/pread_disk_io.cpp
+++ b/src/pread_disk_io.cpp
@@ -271,14 +271,28 @@
 	// storages that have a fence queued behind their outstanding cache writes.
 	// Those writes won't flush on their own (they can be partial pieces the
 	// optimistic pass skips, with the cache under its watermark), so the fence
 	// would wait forever. A generic disk thread flushes each so the writes drain
 	// and the fence can run. Guarded by m_job_mutex.
-	std::vector<std::shared_ptr<aux::pread_storage>> m_fence_flush;
 
 	settings_interface const& m_settings;
 
 	// LRU cache of open files
 	aux::file_pool m_file_pool;
 
+	// storages that have a fence queued behind their outstanding cache writes.
+	// Those writes won't flush on their own (they can be partial pieces the
+	// optimistic pass skips, with the cache under its watermark), so the fence
+	// would wait forever. A generic disk thread flushes each so the writes drain
+	// and the fence can run. Guarded by m_job_mutex.
+	//
+	// Deliberately declared AFTER m_file_pool: members are destroyed in reverse
+	// declaration order and pread_storage::~pread_storage() calls
+	// m_pool.release(), which locks the pool's internal mutex. If this vector
+	// were destroyed after the pool (its original position), a storage still
+	// queued at teardown  -  a session aborted while a fence flush was in flight  - 
+	// would lock the already-destroyed mutex and abort with an uncaught
+	// std::system_error ("mutex lock failed: Invalid argument").
+	std::vector<std::shared_ptr<aux::pread_storage>> m_fence_flush;
+
 	// disk cache
 	aux::disk_buffer_pool m_buffer_pool;
